    "why_no_axis_claim": "phase-cos requires a full day (10-500 uHz) and Earth rotates 360 deg within it, so each baseline sweeps a circle in inertial space during the measurement.  Shuffling which day receives which sidereal rotation leaves the recovered axis unchanged, so the daily statistic carries no celestial right-ascension information and NO alignment claim -- for or against the CMB dipole -- can be made from it.  The declination reflects Earth-fixed network geometry.  Locating the axis needs the seasonal lever Papers 2-3 use: track the anisotropy over 30-day windows across the year and correlate with orbital velocity.",
